<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 8 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Turning-Point Battles</h1><p class="path-tagline">Eight days of fighting on which centuries turned.</p><p class="path-intro">Most battles decide little; a few decide eras. This path examines eight engagements whose outcomes redirected history, not for the drama alone, but for what each reveals about the states that fought and the worlds that followed.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Strategist</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marathon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marathon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Event · 490 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Marathon</span><span class="path-step-why">The Greek line held, and with it the independence that made the classical world possible.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Event · 331 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Gaugamela</span><span class="path-step-why">One afternoon ended two centuries of Persian empire and opened Asia to Alexander.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Event · 31 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Actium</span><span class="path-step-why">The sea battle that ended Rome's civil wars and began its emperors.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Event · 732 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Tours</span><span class="path-step-why">The Frankish victory that fixed the limit of the Arab advance into western Europe.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert"><span class="path-step-ph">5</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1071</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Manzikert</span><span class="path-step-why">The day Anatolia began to turn Turkish, and Byzantium began its long retreat.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1260</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Ain Jalut</span><span class="path-step-why">The Mamluks stopped the Mongols, the first time the conquerors of everywhere were turned back for good.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1571</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Lepanto</span><span class="path-step-why">The last great battle of oared ships broke the spell of Ottoman invincibility at sea.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">Battle of Waterloo</span><span class="path-step-why">The afternoon that closed a quarter-century of world war and set Europe's order for a century.</span></span></a></li></ol>
